Customer orders — 
You open the Nutrigo app or website, choose a restaurant or shop, 
select items, enter the delivery address, and pay online uploading lang ng 
payment proof accept or decline lang ng store 
or choose cash on delivery if available.

Restaurant receives the order — 
Nutrigo sends the order to the restaurant, which accepts it and prepares the food.

A rider is assigned — 
The platform finds an available delivery rider, usually considering factors such as location and availability.

Rider picks it up — 
The rider goes to the restaurant and collects the prepared order.

Delivery — 
The rider follows the delivery information in the app and brings the order to the customer.

Payment and fees — Nutrigo can earn money through restaurant commissions, delivery/service fees